# the SMK-37's keybed (smk37.c): the white keys play the track shown with velocity, never a step (the pads do that);
# the keys outside F3..G5 play too; step record takes the key's velocity; the pedal holds notes; a black key keeps
# the FM-1's job where a page has one (Mix: a track's mute)
wait 300
turn ALGO 1
wait 30
expect trk 2
expect page Steps
# C4 is key 12 (the FM-1's key 7, a white key): it plays, and writes no step
key37 12 down 90
wait 60
expect voices 1
expect note 2 1 1 0
key37 12 up
wait 150
expect voices 0
# an outer key, D3 (key 2): note 50
key37 2 down 80
wait 60
expect voices 1
key37 2 up
wait 150
# step record: REC tapped while stopped; a key writes the cursor step at its velocity, > a rest, < back
tap REC
wait 60
key37 12 down 90
wait 20
key37 12 up
wait 60
expect note 2 1 1 60
expect stepvel 2 1 1 90
key37 2 down 70
wait 20
key37 2 up
wait 60
expect note 2 1 2 50
expect stepvel 2 1 2 70
tap RIGHT
wait 30
key37 16 down 100
wait 20
key37 16 up
wait 60
expect note 2 1 4 64
tap REC
wait 60
# the pedal: a note let go stays until the pedal lifts
pedal down
key37 14 down 100
wait 30
key37 14 up
wait 60
expect voices 1
pedal up
wait 200
expect voices 0
# Mix: black key F#3 (key 6, the FM-1's black key 1) mutes T1 with a tap, as on the FM-1
tap GLO
wait 30
expect page Mix
key37 6 down 100
wait 30
key37 6 up
wait 60
expect mute 1
wait 600
key37 6 down 100
wait 30
key37 6 up
wait 60
expect mute 0
